 "note": "Three-column page. CAFETERIA SUBSTITUTES (22), SCHOOL BUS CONTRACTORS (7), REGULAR BUS DRIVERS (21), SPARE BUS DRIVERS (13), SCHOOL VOLUNTEERS (9). Substitutes, contractors and drivers -> district-wide; volunteers -> unknown (not staff; kept because named, dept marks them). Column assignment of drivers is by position and by the printed counts (21 regular, 13 spare); the unsorted order of a few names (A. R. Paton, R. Warpula) makes the regular/spare split of those two a best fit, not certain. Substitute columns: col1 Baker..Estabrooks (8), col2 Farnham..Padula (9), col3 Racine..Vaillancourt (5) = 22. Mrs. dropped; the (Effective 1/27/75) notes belong to Cannavino and Vaillancourt. Bus numbers on following lines are in role_raw.  Integration pass, 31 Oct 2026: school bus contractors, drivers and volunteers moved from entries to ignored (not school staff; every 1971-1980 page treated alike), and `middle` written `turkey-hill` -- the 1972 and 1974 listings print the building as `Turkey Hill Middle School (Grades 5-7)`, the town's one middle school."
